  </sharedSelectionEntryGroups><sharedRules><rule id="5093-098d-a6e2-9246" name="Standard Bearer" hidden="false">
      <description>Any Imperial Guard units with a model within 12" of the Standard Bearer may re-roll any failed Morale checks.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="16d3-73ab-2527-3e33" name="Medi-pack" hidden="false">
      <description>Medi-packs allow a unit with a medic to ignore the first failed saving throw it rolls in every turn. The medi-pack may not be used on any model which suffers instant death or that has been hit by a close combat weapon that allows no Amrour save. It may not be used if the medic is in base contact with an enemy model.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="fcaa-7305-6950-d142" name="Comm-Link" hidden="false">
      <description>If a Command HQ or Command Section has a comm-link, then one squad with a comm-link each turn can use the Officer’s Leadership value no matter where they are on the battlefield (normally they’d have to be within 12"). You can use the comm-link anytime, such as right before a Leadership test or even if the command unit is still in reserve.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="bfa6-639a-4ff4-e20e" name="Master-crafted Weapons" hidden="false">
      <description>The bearer may re-roll one failed to hit roll per turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="0630-f0bd-6da5-e593" name="Trademark Item" hidden="false">
      <description>A unit led by a person who carries a trademark item may re-roll any failed Morale or Pinning checks it suffers. However, if the character is slain, the unit must pass a Morale test to avoid falling back.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="c061-bcf5-ed69-d507" name="Scanner" hidden="false">
      <description>If enemy infiltrators set up with 4D6" of a model with a surveyor then the model is allowed to take a 'free' shot at them. If the model is part of a unit, the whole unit may shoot. These shots are taken before the battle begins and may cause the infiltrators to fall back.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="468c-bd45-5505-589a" name="Immobile" hidden="false">
      <description>Once deployed, the model may not be moved unless towed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="f779-54b0-691f-402d" name="Amphibious" hidden="false">
      <description>Treat all water features as clear terrain when moving</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="3113-8762-7d4c-7334" name="Anti-Air" hidden="false">
      <description>Roll to hit aircraft using the firers normal BS</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8573-0653-d612-e4de" name="Smoke Launchers" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per game, after completing movement, a vehicle with smoke launchers may trigger them. The vehicle cannot fire and use its smoke launchers in the same turn. Any penetrating hits scored by the enemy in the next Shooting phase count as glancing hits.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="4877-41b8-d9e1-6da3" name="Searchlight" hidden="false">
      <description>During Night Fighting missions, one enemy unit spotted by the vehicle can be fired at by any other Imperial Guard units in range and with line of fire. However, the vehicle using the Searchlight will then be exposed and can be fired at by any enemy units that are in range and line of sight of it until the next turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="11ff-f612-addd-577e" name="Leadership" hidden="false" />
    <rule id="7023-343a-0f96-bd4e" name="Rough Terrain Modification" hidden="false">
      <description>A vehicle that moves no more than 6" may re-rolled failed Difficult Terrain tests</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="647d-f731-5d52-f8e4" name="Camo Cloak" hidden="false">
      <description>Any Tanith squad adds +1 to any cover saves they are allowed. In addition, opponents roll 2D6x2 instead of 2D6x3 when attempting to spot Tanith troops in a Night Fight.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="36d3-c20f-b78f-7bf9" name="Tanith Knife" hidden="false">
      <description>A unit led by a person who carries a trademark item may re-roll any failed Morale or Pinning checks it suffers. However, if the character is slain, the unit must pass a Morale test to avoid falling back.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="ea86-cee4-a47b-c214" name="Absolute Direction" hidden="false">
      <description>All Tanith units may re-roll failed Reserve rolls. If a Tanith unit is affected by a result on the Alaitoc Ranger Disruption table from Codex: Craftworld Eldar, roll a dice, the result is ignored on the roll of a 4+.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="bcc1-8c37-a9c9-b60b" name="Holy Relic" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per battle. On any turn the model with the relic does not move they may reveal it. All friendly models that are within 2D6" gain +1 Attacks for the rest of that turn. The relic may be revealed in the opposing player's turn assuming the model with the relic did not move in the previous turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1973-df4c-dfdf-8af6" name="Bionics" hidden="false">
      <description>When a model with bionics is killed, instead place it on its side. Roll a D6 at the start of the next turn: on a roll of 6 the model stands back up with 1 wound, but on any other roll it is removed as a casualty.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="f1bf-49f9-4094-c2f9" name="Carapace Armor" hidden="false">
      <description>4+ Armour Save</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="b3db-ab15-ba69-979f" name="Refractor Field" hidden="false">
      <description>Gain a 5+ invulnerable save</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1c37-d83d-2234-7c18" name="Targeter" hidden="false">
      <description>Models equipped with a targeter are allowed to pre-measure the range to a target before they decide who to shoot at in the Shooting phase. This ability must be used after all Guess ranged weapons have been used this turn, otherwise those weapons cannot fire this turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="23bf-b1d4-efd9-39e9" name="Iron Discipline" hidden="false">
      <description>Any unit using the Leadership ability of a Cadian Officer with the Iron Discipline ability for Morale or Pinning test ignores the -1 modifier for being under half strength and may regroup even if below half strength.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="0a5e-9493-a5b1-e5d5" name="Sharpshooters" hidden="false">
      <description>Any Cadian infantry model with a BS of 3 may make a single re-roll of a shooting to hit roll of 1. This has no effect when firing plasma weapons or sniper rifles.</description>
    </rule>
  <rule id="0b0d-c34d-0b36-560d" name="Deathworld Veterans" hidden="false">
      <description>Deathworld Veterans count woods or jungles as clear terrain. They receive a 4+ cover save for being in woods or jungle terrain. If they do not move in the movement phase may see and shoot through 12" of woods or jungle terrain instead of the normal 6". And they may infiltrate into woods or jungle in missions where infiltration is allowed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="32a8-a559-293a-a999" name="Opps, Sorry Sir!" hidden="false">
      <description>Roll a D6 for each Commissar before setting them up. On a roll of 1 the commissar has suffered an accident and cannot be used.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1e9a-8f2f-238e-9e34" name="Ambush" hidden="false">
      <description>See rules for Ambush set-up in Codex: Catachan page 20</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="9d60-b109-f37e-cfa6" name="Gung Ho" hidden="false">
      <description>The unit may re-roll failed Morale and Pinning tests and can try to regroup even if below half strength.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1496-27c3-2f58-885c" name="Deathworld Toxins" hidden="false">
      <description>Deathworld Snipers may re-roll a failed roll to wound when using their rifles.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="2150-cbd0-329c-5f33" name="Camouflage" hidden="false">
      <description>Deathworld Snipers have a 3+ cover save in woods or jungle terrain.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="f24f-9916-55fe-8bf6" name="Disappear" hidden="false">
      <description>Snipers never move. During your Movement phase, you may remove the sniper, representing the Sniper merging back into the shadows. Once removed, a Sniper may not return to the battlefield but doesn't count as having been killed for Victory point purposes. Snipers cannot claim table quarters or other objectives and don't have to be killed for an attacker to win Meat Grinder or Grand Assault.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="e3ad-147a-43f5-a00a" name="Set-Up" hidden="false">
      <description>See rules for Booby Trap set-up in Codex: Catachan page 21</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="ef50-ea59-9c80-ccd7" name="Ignore Cover Saves" hidden="false">
      <description>Ignore cover saves.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1644-75b3-7a1b-6398" name="Pinning" hidden="false">
      <description>Any unit that suffers one or more casualties from a booby trap must test for pinning.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="dc13-2a4b-c609-d6da" name="Plasma Charge" hidden="false">
      <description>The model that triggered the charge is hit automatically.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8879-cace-77eb-a230" name="Shredder Mine" hidden="false">
      <description>The mine is located D6" away from the model that triggered it, in the direction indicated by the arrow on the Scatter dice. The player who laid the mine may place the flamer template with the narrow end at the location of the mine and positioned in such a manner that the model who triggered the trap is at least partially under the template. Any models touched by the template are hit automatically.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="3d45-8e04-2e94-1f6d" name="Spring Mine" hidden="false">
      <description>Place the large Ordnance Blast marker so that the central hole is over the model which triggered the trap. Then roll for scatter in the same way as you would for ordnance. Any models that are fully under the Ordnance Blast marker are hit automatically, and any that are partially under the Blast marker are hit on a 4+.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8e6a-cb86-d10e-8502" name="Trap" hidden="false">
      <description>Place the small Blast market so that the central hole is over the model that triggered the trap. Any models fully under the Blast marker are hit automatically and any partially under are hit on a 4+.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="0f0f-2dd1-567e-7c66" name="Placement" hidden="false">
      <description>Each booby trap you take allows you to booby trap a 1' square area.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="5129-ecf7-d3f2-2a76" name="Jungle Fighters" hidden="false">
      <description>Roll 3D6 and pick the highest to see how far the unit can move through jungle terrain. When pursuing and falling back through difficult terrain, they roll 3D6 and halve the result. They only become 'spooked' on a roll of a triple one and only set off booby traps on any roll of a triple.
They receive a 4+ cover save for being in woods or jungle.
They may infiltrate into woods or jungles in missions where infiltration is allowed.</description>
    </rule>
  <rule id="53c9-3f47-f245-64d0" name="Ork Hunters" hidden="false">
      <description>Ork Hunters alway shit Orks on a 3+ in close combat.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="32c7-9250-c6eb-edca" name="To Know The Enemy" hidden="false">
      <description>When a squad of Armageddon Ork Hunters charges into close combat check its size by rolling 2D6. If the score is equal or less than the number of Armageddon Ork Hunters in the squad, they charge in with a rousing warcry to rival that to the Orks they fight. All Ork Hunters in the squad double their Initiative for the rest of the assault phase.</description>
    </rule>
  <rule id="0aa2-ad12-6696-1869" name="City Fighters" hidden="false">
      <description>If this unit is in cover then its cover saving throw is increased by +1 point.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="152e-3207-7d66-4964" name="Tank Hunters" hidden="false">
      <description>The unit always passes any tests for tank shock and adds +1 to all Armour Penetration rolls.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="28fc-a0b2-82ae-14c6" name="Citizens" hidden="false">
      <description>You may reroll any reserve rolls for this unit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8fd7-c2ff-1577-b5d0" name="Sewer Rats" hidden="false">
      <description>The unit can use the special rules for Subterranean Movement to deploy, even in scenarios where these rules are not normally used.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="d99b-425a-ce2d-e136" name="Stealthy" hidden="false">
      <description>This unit may set up using the infiltrator rules. If infiltrators are not allowed in the scenario being played then the unit may make a free move immediately after both sides have deployed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="48e9-280b-8702-e4d7" name="Cunning" hidden="false">
      <description>This unit may set up one booby-trap of your choice each game using the rules in the Cityfight book.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="a39a-0e41-19fe-c0e8" name="Cityfight Veterans" hidden="false">
      <description>Cityfight Veterans may always roll one extra dice for their difficult terrain tests in the city.
Cityfight Veterans who do not move during the movement phase reduce their target's cover save by -1 in addition to any other modifiers.</description>
    </rule>
  <rule id="d5f7-46ce-8768-3e81" name="Hardened Fighters" hidden="false">
      <description>The Death Korp may ignore negative modifiers for Morale checks and tests for regrouping.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="c9cc-854b-30e2-0c2c" name="Death Before Dishonour" hidden="false">
      <description>Death Korp troops are Fearless in close combat, automatically passing any Morale checks they are required to make, and will carry on fighting until they have beaten their foes or until they are all dead. Additionally, the must Sweeping Advance after an enemy that falls back.</description>
    </rule>
  <rule id="52f1-333b-4047-dc5c" name="On Time, On Target" hidden="false" />
    <rule id="3a78-7801-651a-d159" name="Gung Ho" hidden="false" />
  <rule id="56bd-9279-b9df-5645" name="Scavengers" hidden="false">
      <description>Savlar Chem-Dogs may never make a sweeping advance after a combat.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="c75e-7f7f-5409-bb7f" name="Nitro-Chem Inhaler" hidden="false">
      <description>Savlar Chem-Dogs ignore negative modifiers to their Morale checks, and will test on the unmodified Leadership of the unit or character that is leading it all times.
In addition, if they do fail a Morale check, they will become pinned instead of falling back. However, they fall back in close combat as normal.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="b0df-bc87-7a32-f38d" name="Chem-Riders" hidden="false">
      <description>All Savlar Chem-Riders benefit from an Invulnerable 5+ save.</description>
    </rule>
  <rule name="Medallion Crimson" id="ed22-fd2d-2ed7-c027" hidden="false">
      <description>The first time the bearer is wounded by an attack that causes instant death he takes a single wound instead.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Macharian Cross" id="32d4-2523-00ba-3a64" hidden="false">
      <description>After deployment is complete, but before determining who has first turn, any single infantry squad (including Hardended Veterans, Storm Troopers, Ogryns, Ratlings, Infantry Platoon squads and Armour Fist Squads, but not any vehicles) within 6" of the Officer may be redeployed up to 12, but must abide by all the mission's deployment zones and rules.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Carapace Armor" id="b894-c44c-ccf7-481b" hidden="false">
      <description>4+ Armour Save</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Bionics" id="a5a1-c9f5-36b8-b3ee" hidden="false">
      <description>When a model with bionics is killed, instead place it on its side. Roll a D6 at the start of the next turn: on a roll of 6 the model stands back up with 1 wound, but on any other roll it is removed as a casualty.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Camo-Cloak" id="5146-a032-a0dc-383e" hidden="false">
      <description>The unit adds +1 to any cover save already allowed</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Advisor" id="4ac0-5e0f-ed0b-1910" hidden="false">
      <description>Commissars, Priests and Sanctioned Psykers are Advisors. For each type of Advisor, one must be assigned to the Command HQ. Any others of that type are then allocated to Platoon HQ squads. If all Command and Platoon HQ squads have an Advisor of that type, then the remainder join infantry squads, armoured first squads or storm trooper squads.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Vox-Caster" id="1c1f-a642-487e-047c" hidden="false">
      <description>If a unit containing an Officer has a vo-xcaster, then one squad per turn that also has a vox-caster may use the Leadership ability of the officer regardless of distance. The benefits of standards and trademark items are not conveyed through the vox-caster</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Master Vox-Caster" id="7cff-18d6-5084-12d1" hidden="false">
      <description>Any number of squads may use the Leadership of the HQ's Officier for a single Morale or Leadership tests rather than the usual limit of one allowed with a Vox-Caster.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Regimental Standard" id="95fa-f514-ada8-6581" hidden="false">
      <description>Add +1 to the combat resolution of any assault that takes place at least within 6" of the regimental standard. A Regimental Standard also counts as a Company Standard.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Refractor Field" id="23d9-53b8-2ee6-bcc4" hidden="false">
      <description>Gain a 5+ invulnerable save</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Iron Discipline" id="372b-640d-9314-4d15" hidden="false">
      <description>Any unit using the Leadership ability of an Officer or Senior Officer with Iron Discipline ignore the -1 modifier for being under half strength and may regroup even if below half strength.

Incompatible with: Chem-inhalers</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Trademark Item" id="fe9d-b2e5-9848-930d" hidden="false">
      <description>A unit led by a person who carries a trademark item may re-roll any failed Morale or Pinning checks it suffers. However, if the character is slain, the unit must pass a Morale test to avoid falling back.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="It's For Your Own Good!" id="dc4b-c001-e685-417b" hidden="false">
      <description>If a Sanctioned Psyker attached to the same unit as a Commissar suffers a Perils of the Warp attack, the Commissar will immediately execute him to prevent him from being possessed. Remove the Psyker as a casualty without triggering the power or the Perils of the Warp.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Die-hards" id="1d6d-e7a1-d98a-9774" hidden="false">
      <description>Do not count negative Moral modifiers for being outnumbered in close combat.

Incompatible with: Chem-inhalers</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Hardened Fighters" id="026a-7921-617f-0f9f" hidden="false">
      <description>Gain +1 to WS. Sentinels additionally gain +1 A.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Jungle Fighters" id="fc84-fd6e-473d-87b5" hidden="false">
      <description>Gain the following:
- Can see 12" through forest or jungle terrain

- Receive a 4+ Cover save when in forest or jungle terrain

- Move full speed through forest or jungle terrain

- May infiltrate if the mission permits if they can deploy into forest or jungle terrain

- May include a Heavy Flamer instead of Heavy Weapon, but can never take lascannons

- Reduce armour to 6+</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Close Order Drill" id="6983-e7af-4750-8ce1" hidden="false">
      <description>If the unit has all units in base to base contact with each other then the models in the unit gain +1 Leadership and +1 Initiative.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Light Infantry" id="9c9b-0b1e-5e94-d5ca" hidden="false">
      <description>Any unit without a Chimera:
- Rolls 2D6 and take the highest for moving through difficult terrain

- May infiltrate

- May take a sniper rifle instead of a heavy weapon</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Sharpshooters" id="83da-2c7d-ec06-4d91" hidden="false">
      <description>Any Guard infantry model with a BS 3 may re-roll to hit rolls of 1. May not be used on Plasma weapons or Sniper Rifles.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Xeno-Fighters" id="2f2b-c4c0-f256-0696" hidden="false">
      <description>Xeno-fighters hit on a 3+ regardless of respoective Weapon Skill values against their preferred enemy. This advantage does not apply against Independent Characters, Tyranid Monstrous Creatures, or Monstrous Creatures.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Chem-inhaler" id="5941-d0ec-c7c3-1a8c" hidden="false">
      <description>The unit will always test Morale, Leadership or Pinning with no negative modifiers. If they fail a Morale check for 25% shooting casualties, they will be pinned rather than fall back.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Cameleonline" id="63fd-b2df-2c9a-ffc9" hidden="false">
      <description>The unit adds +1 to any cover save already allowed</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Cyber-Enhancement" id="627d-af3d-810d-5a41" hidden="false">
      <description>Gain invulnerable save of 6+</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Warrior Weapons" id="cea3-fcb7-8609-2c7d" hidden="false">
      <description>Replace lasguns with laspistols and close combat weapons</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Telepathic Order" id="be70-60f1-070f-c7ba" hidden="false">
      <description>The Psyker extends the zone of influence of an Officer he is accompanying. Use at the start of the Imperial Guard turn. If the test is passed, the Leadership radius of the Officer in the same squad as the Psyker is extended to 18" until the start of the next Imperial Guard turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Psychic Ward" id="8967-38e7-893a-8596" hidden="false">
      <description>If a psychic power would normally affect the Sanctioned Psyker or the unit he is accompanying, make a Psychic test. If the test is passed then roll a D6. On a 4+ the power is cancelled.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Psychic Lash" id="1da3-c105-b700-5fc8" hidden="false">
      <description>Make a Psychic test at the start of the Imperial Guard Assault phase. If successful, the power remains in phase until the start of the next Imperial Guard Assault phase. The Psyker's may choose to use the Lash in place of its normal attacks. The Psyker gets D3 Attacks (with no bonuses) at Strength 3, with any wounds ignoring Armour saves.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Machine Curse" id="d2dd-9386-2ebe-dc40" hidden="false">
      <description>Make the Psychic test at the start of the Assault phase. If passed the power is effective until the end of the same Assault phase. Make one close combat attack against a vehicle in base contact with the Psyker. If a hit is scored, roll a D6:
1 - 3: No effect
4 - 5: Inflict Glancing Hit
6 : Inflict Penetrating Hit</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Amphibious" id="8af5-ea0c-2a76-26d8" hidden="false">
      <description>Treat all water features as clear terrain when moving</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Improved Comms" id="b71b-97b6-7ac6-b71f" hidden="false">
      <description>The Imperial Guard player may re-roll one Reserves roll per turn, and to re-roll the dice when checking to see if an enemy unit or obstacle is hit by a preliminary bombardment</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Immobile" id="de3d-c21c-3d4f-5259" hidden="false">
      <description>Once deployed, the model may not be moved unless towed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Anti-Air" id="2dca-27d7-d779-65f4" hidden="false">
      <description>Roll to hit aircraft using the firers normal BS</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="VTOL Hover Mode" id="c28e-05cc-afdf-32d0" hidden="false">
      <description>Rather than leave the table as per normal, the flyer may choose to engage is VTOL Hover mode to remain on the table. It remains stationary, but can turn in any direction to bring its weapons to bear. It may fire all of its weapons.
For the purposes of being fired at, the vehicle counts as a moving Skimmer. It can therefore be fired at using the firer's normal BS. All hits are treated as glancing hits. It can only be attack in close combat by attackers that can fly or have jump packs, in which case it is treated as a moving vehicle.
If the vehicle is immobilised the model is destroyed.
At the end of its own turn, the vehicle may disengage VTOL. It not reverts to being a flyer. It cannot return in the enemy turn immediately afer it leaves the table.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Searchlight" id="f055-41c4-5db5-4372" hidden="false">
      <description>During Night Fighting missions, one enemy unit spotted by the vehicle can be fired at by any other Imperial Guard units in range and with line of fire. However, the vehicle using the Searchlight will then be exposed and can be fired at by any enemy units that are in range and line of sight of it until the next turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Smoke Launchers" id="51f3-87b2-5634-c751" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per game, after completing movement, a vehicle with smoke launchers may trigger them. The vehicle cannot fire and use its smoke launchers in the same turn. Any penetrating hits scored by the enemy in the next Shooting phase count as glancing hits.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Medi-pack" id="9539-38c4-b60d-9e8c" hidden="false">
      <description>Medi-packs allow a unit with a medic to ignore the first failed saving throw it rolls in every turn. The medi-pack may not be used on any model which suffers instant death or that has been hit by a close combat weapon that allows no Amrour save. It may not be used if the medic is in base contact with an enemy model.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Skilled Driver" id="d551-bb27-b00f-3992" hidden="false">
      <description>You can re-roll the dice for crossing difficult ground. You must abide by the re-roll result even if it is worse.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Night Fighters" id="1912-32c6-0d4a-00ba" hidden="false">
      <description>The crew may re-roll the dice when rolling to determine how far they can see in a Night Fight scenario. You must abide by the re-roll result even if it is worse.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ace Gunner" id="f3fc-c8af-3ee8-8b59" hidden="false">
      <description>The gunner has an eye for finding weak spots. After rolling to hit, the gunner may add +1 to the Armour Penetration roll against vehicles.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Disciplined Crew" id="cf4e-d06c-edc7-6b74" hidden="false">
      <description>Treat 'Crew Stunned' results as 'Crew Shaken' instead.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Gung-ho! Crew" id="4c94-e6d8-9a97-ec88" hidden="false">
      <description>An enemy infantry unit forced to take a Tank Shock test by this vehicle does so at -1 to their Leadership</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Battle Hardened Crew" id="a2b2-884e-683f-b7fd" hidden="false">
      <description>If the vehicle takes a Crew Shaken result, then roll a D6. On a 4+ ignore the result.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Veteran Commander" id="5616-80b5-25b7-3c31" hidden="false">
      <description>The commander gives the tank a single re-roll for the battle. This re-roll can be used on any one D6 roll which relates to the tank's action. This could be crossing difficult terrain, hitting or wounding with a weapon, etc. Note it is only a single dice, so it cannot re-roll all the hits from a weapon, only one. It cannot be used Scatter dice and cannot be used to force an opponent to re-roll a D6.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Slick Loader" id="dbf0-ebc7-7687-c139" hidden="false">
      <description>If the vehicle remains stationary it may fire its main weapon twice in one turn. The second shot must be at the same target as the first. It cannot fire any other weapons. This skill can only be used on Ordnance weapons.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Leadership" id="d39b-40d5-efdc-5be0" hidden="false">
      <description>Any Imperial Guard squad within 12" of the officer may use his Leadership value for all Morale and Pinning tests.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Armoured Crew Compartment" id="d1bf-5c7d-17b2-eda3" hidden="false">
      <description>The vehicle no longer counts as being open-topped.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Camo Netting" id="a0a6-24fc-5ff7-29c4" hidden="false">
      <description>In scenarios using the Hidden Set-up rules, vehicles carrying camo netting can be set up hidden anywhere in their deployment zone.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Extra Armour" id="0d41-84e8-e76b-8cfb" hidden="false">
      <description>Count the 'Crew Stunned' result as 'Crew Shaken' instead</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Mine Sweeper" id="46fc-5d60-1c97-064d" hidden="false">
      <description>The vehicle may enter a minefield without being attack. Any minefield the vehicle moves across is cleared and removed from play</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Rough Terrain Modification" id="11b9-8531-3d08-faec" hidden="false">
      <description>A vehicle that moves no more than 6" may re-rolled failed Difficult Terrain tests</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Track Guards" id="52e7-9ed5-7aab-0790" hidden="false">
      <description>The vehicle treats 'Immobilised' results as 'Crew Stunned' on a roll of a 4+. This does not combine with the extra armour ability.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Company Standard" id="fc76-2e13-78f0-6d51" hidden="false">
      <description>Units of Imperial Guard Infantry with a model within 12" of the standard can re-roll failed Morale tests.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Holy Relic" id="a089-b263-ac69-013e" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per battle. On any turn the model with the relic does not move they may reveal it. All friendly models that are within 2D6" gain +1 Attacks for the rest of that turn. The relic may be revealed in the opposing player's turn assuming the model with the relic did not move in the previous turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Honorifica Imperialis" id="a69f-c203-1d8d-f001" hidden="false">
      <description>The wearer gains the stats of a Heroic Senior Officer, but does not become an officer or an independent character</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Master-crafted Weapons" id="0e54-6618-9b31-0f81" hidden="false">
      <description>The bearer may re-roll one failed to hit roll per turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Purity Seals" id="4704-e2b7-e2e7-bbb5" hidden="false">
      <description>If a model wearing seals falls back, roll one extra D6 for Fall Back distance, and then discard the dice of your choice. If the model is part of a unit this ability applies to the whole unit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Rosarius" id="76de-0663-998d-64bf" hidden="false">
      <description>Gain a 4+ Invulnerable save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Signum" id="24e8-78a1-aed9-90ba" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per turn, re-roll one missed to hit shooting roll for the Techpriest or one of his attendant Servitors</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Surveyor" id="eb6e-5162-ade5-a2ed" hidden="false">
      <description>If enemy infiltrators set up with 4D6" of a model with a surveyor then the model is allowed to take a 'free' shot at them. If the model is part of a unit, the whole unit may shoot. These shots are taken before the battle begins and may cause the infiltrators to fall back.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Targeter" id="0a02-59d7-63e7-b752" hidden="false">
      <description>Models equipped with a targeter are allowed to pre-measure the range to a target before they decide who to shoot at in the Shooting phase. This ability must be used after all Guess ranged weapons have been used this turn, otherwise those weapons cannot fire this turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Drop Troops" id="4e41-96aa-ff64-3ba9" hidden="false">
      <description>Any Infantry units or Sentinels may Deep Strike if the mission permits.

Incompatible with Warrior Weapons</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Grenadiers" id="d687-818c-b8d4-b06d" hidden="false">
      <description>0-3 Storm Trooper squads can be taken as Troops, but can't Deep Strike or Infiltrate

Incompatible with: Warrior Weapons</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Mechanised" id="ebd3-2c10-342-2d96" hidden="false">
      <description>All Infantry units must take a Chimera transport


Incompatible with: Warrior Weapons, Light Infantry</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Independent Commissars" id="4a40-dc0d-6b30-d221" hidden="false">
      <description>A squad of 1-3 Commissars may be taken as an Elite choice</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Veterans" id="817a-f531-5d74-7a9c" hidden="false">
      <description>Exempt from standard 0-1 limit on Hardened Veterans</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Priests" id="4ea9-fdf2-4697-e007" hidden="false">
      <description>Allows the use of Priests</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Techpriest Enginseers" id="a1cb-114c-9a8e-cffd" hidden="false">
      <description>Allows the use of Techpriest Enginseers</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Sanctioned Psykers" id="f3ff-352f-3d69-14fb" hidden="false">
      <description>Allows the use of Sanctioned Psykers</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ratling Squads" id="2ffe-68dd-3690-d600" hidden="false">
      <description>Allows the use of Ratling Squads</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ogryn Squads" id="3dcf-9a49-9299-3cc7" hidden="false">
      <description>Allows the use of Ogryn Squads</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Special Weapon Squads" id="9ec4-6010-77a3-19e5" hidden="false">
      <description>Allows the use of Special Weapon Squads</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Conscript Platoons" id="6588-16a9-e3ab-85e2" hidden="false">
      <description>Allows the use of Conscript Platoons</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Rough Rider Squadrons" id="9ad0-1355-3699-c65e" hidden="false">
      <description>Allows the use of Rough Rider Squadrons</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Heavy Weapon Platoons" id="e1c7-7fbf-571-d95d" hidden="false">
      <description>Allows the use of Heavy Weapon Platoons</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Storm Trooper Squads" id="cb33-92f-be9a-53eb" hidden="false">
      <description>Allows the use of Storm Trooper Squads</description>
    </rule>
  <rule name="Reconnaissance" id="4572-3720-10ae-12f5" hidden="false">
      <description>The reconnaissance mission grants the Scouts and Move Through Cover special rules</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Airborne Assault" id="6244-8629-df8e-2b3d" hidden="false">
      <description>The airborne assault mission allows the Storm Trooper squad to re-roll the scatter dice when they deep strike.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Behind Enemy Lines" id="bad3-cdf9-b489-99eb" hidden="false">
      <description>The behind enemy lines mission grants the squad infiltrate special rule and their weapons count as Pinning the first time the squad fires.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Look Out - Arghh!" id="c50b-ca51-2909-c0d7" hidden="false">
      <description>Whilst a Bodyguard is alive, each time the Command Squad is wounded by the enemy, up to two wounds allocated to the Company Commander are instead resolved against the Bodyguard(s).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Unique Senior Officer" id="e3eb-5eda-1ba9-14d6" hidden="false">
      <description>One Company Command Squad in your army may replace it's Company Commander with this model</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Unique Junior Officer" id="8df4-090c-0bf9-8aae" hidden="false">
      <description>One Platoon Command Squad in your army may replace its Platoon Commander with this model.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules><sharedProfiles><profile id="c623-489e-d7a0-0a93" name="Captain" hidden="false" typeId="1e16-2bd8-7cad-379b" typeName="Unit">
